{"content":[{"c":["BEN* (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Levite musician appointed by King David (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.18","r":"1Chr.15.18","rawR":"1Chr.15.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.18","value":"1Chr.15.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:18"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). The Masoretic Text (the OT as annotated by medieval Hebrew scholars) and the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," include the name Ben, but the Septuagint (ancient Greek translation of the OT) and modern versions omit it because it is missing in verses ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.20","r":"1Chr.15.20","rawR":"1Chr.15.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.20","value":"1Chr.15.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"20"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.21","r":"1Chr.15.21","rawR":"1Chr.15.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.21","value":"1Chr.15.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"21"},". Since the Masoretic Text also omits it in the later verses, the inclusion of Ben in verse ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.18","r":"1Chr.15.18","rawR":"1Chr.15.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.18","value":"1Chr.15.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"18"}," may be a scribal error."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BenPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 15:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.18","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.18","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.18"},{"anchorText":"20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.20","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.20","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.20"},{"anchorText":"21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.21","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.21","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.21"},{"anchorText":"18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_